      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Flaky tests in a containerized environment are often caused by environmental inconsistencies, like timing issues or resource contention, which can be particularly tricky to debug. You might be dealing with race conditions, network latency spikes, or resource starvation within your containers. To track these down, start by adding more granular logging around the test execution, and try running the tests repeatedly in isolation to see if the pattern of failure is consistent under specific load conditions. Sometimes, introducing deliberate, small delays in your tests can help expose these timing-dependent bugs, which is a good way to narrow down the scope of the problem.",
      "source": "target",
